Ticket [#4471](https://github.com/RadoslawZuchowski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues) was marked known as one parser problem. The exported reports show **two distinct causes** among 412 unique reports. The archive has overlapping pages, so repeated report IDs are counted once.

## The problems

### Day-first dates parsed month-first · 379 reports

The shared parser reads month first. For tenants whose locale writes the day before the month, this can swap the day and month, causing bookings and reminders to land on the wrong day. These 379 reports cover all 11 tenants and span 1 April to 4 October 2026.

Track this cause in [issue #1](https://github.com/RadoslawZuchowski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

### booking-v3 hint conflicts with day-first tenant dates · 33 reports

Three day-first tenants use booking-v3, whose field hint says `MM/DD/YYYY`. People follow that hint, but the form interprets their entry in the tenant's day-first order. This is a separate form-hint problem, not the shared parser bug. The 33 reports span 17 April to 22 September 2026.

Track this cause in [issue #2](https://github.com/RadoslawZuchowski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

## Recount the ticket

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The intake tag is only a guess; classify each report using its tenant locale, booking form, and channel. Keep the two causes in separate tickets so each fix can be tracked independently.

